# The ephemeris asset is binary, and that must be said explicitly.
#
# A Windows client with core.autocrlf=true "fixes" line endings by default.
# Inside an array of doubles the sequence 0x0D 0x0A occurs regularly, so
# without this line the asset could quietly corrupt on clone and the
# cross-platform comparison (ROADMAP C5) would fail on Windows for a
# spectacularly obscure reason.
*.eph binary

# Scripts must stay LF: under sh a CRLF file simply does not run.
*.sh text eol=lf
